<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka T-bill yields continue to ease.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka T-bill yields continue to ease.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average yields of three, six and 12-month treasury bills yields decreased by 0.13 percentge points, 0.25 and 0.59 at Wednesday's auctions, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>		   Bids received   Bids accepted   Avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months     2,421	     2,081	  10.87 (11.00)</p>
<p>    6 months     1,336		 356	  11.61 (11.86)</p>
<p>    12 months    6,585	     1,315	  11.99 (12.58)</p>
<p>    Total	 10,342	     3,752</p>
<p>NOTE - Bids in million rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets).</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
